1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,307
Strike: weekly options vaults for Robinhood Chain stock tokens.

2
00:00:03,307 --> 00:00:08,141
Live on Robinhood Chain testnet: real events, read from the chain.

3
00:00:08,141 --> 00:00:12,323
Stock tokens on Robinhood Chain earn nothing on their own.

4
00:00:12,323 --> 00:00:16,225
Options exist on the chain, but people run them by hand.

5
00:00:16,225 --> 00:00:20,145
Strike: an AI agent runs the vault, and the contract enforces the rules.

6
00:00:20,145 --> 00:00:25,466
The mandate playground: ask the deployed contract about a proposal. No wallet.

7
00:00:25,466 --> 00:00:30,733
Honest agent: a 0.20-delta call. The contract answers: Accepted.

8
00:00:30,733 --> 00:00:35,772
Reckless agent: an at-the-money put. Rejected: DeltaOutOfBand.

9
00:00:35,772 --> 00:00:41,797
The slash: 10 USDG of the agent's bond, paid to the vault's depositors.

10
00:00:41,797 --> 00:00:47,529
Each verdict is a read-only call to the deployed EpochManager, not a simulation.

11
00:00:47,529 --> 00:00:50,792
A real epoch on Robinhood Chain testnet, 29 Sep 2026. First, the seller agent.

12
00:00:50,792 --> 00:00:52,892
The seller agent targets a 0.20-delta call on the TSLA covered-call vault.

13
00:00:52,892 --> 00:00:54,806
proposeByDelta: the contract solves the strike on-chain.

14
00:00:54,806 --> 00:00:58,247
Accepted at a $369.86 strike. The series goes on sale.

15
00:00:58,247 --> 00:01:02,817
--reckless: the agent forces an at-the-money put, outside the 0.10 to 0.35 delta band.

16
00:01:02,817 --> 00:01:04,829
Rejected on-chain: DeltaOutOfBand. 10 USDG of the agent's bond is slashed.

17
00:01:04,829 --> 00:01:06,834
The agent's bond drops from 60 to 50 USDG: 1 of 3 strikes.

18
00:01:06,834 --> 00:01:11,137
The rejection on Blockscout: proposeSeries, and 10 USDG moved out of the agent's bond.

19
00:01:11,137 --> 00:01:15,770
A buyer agent spends up to 15 USDG on the live series.

20
00:01:15,770 --> 00:01:19,075
It bought 4 calls for 10.005944 USDG. The premium is the most it can lose.

21
00:01:19,075 --> 00:01:22,760
The TSLA covered-call vault, live on testnet. It holds 5 testnet TSLA.

22
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:28,999
This week's series: a TSLA call at $369.86, expiring Fri Oct 2. All 4 sold.

23
00:01:28,999 --> 00:01:35,516
The buy price: spot plus 0.5% against the buyer, at Black-Scholes fair value, never below intrinsic.

24
00:01:35,516 --> 00:01:42,133
Buyer profits above $372.36. At or below $369.86, depositors keep the full premium.

25
00:01:42,133 --> 00:01:46,265
Epoch 1 opened Tue Sep 29 and settles at Friday's NYSE close.

26
00:01:46,265 --> 00:01:49,150
Every agent posts a USDG bond. A rejected proposal costs 10 USDG.

27
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:54,883
Agent #1: ERC-8004 identity #114, 1 accepted, 1 rejected, 1 strike, 50 USDG bond.

28
00:01:54,883 --> 00:01:58,615
The rejection feed: DeltaOutOfBand on the TSLA put vault, 10 USDG slashed.

29
00:01:58,615 --> 00:02:01,559
The Telegram bot reads the chain's logs and posts an alert for each event.

30
00:02:01,559 --> 00:02:05,990
A rejected proposal: the rule it broke, the 10 USDG slash and the transaction.

31
00:02:05,990 --> 00:02:09,742
A sale: 4 TSLA calls bought for 10.005944 USDG.

32
00:02:09,742 --> 00:02:13,026
The safety monitor: every Robinhood Chain stock token, read live from mainnet.

33
00:02:13,026 --> 00:02:17,040
Each token gets the verdict the contracts would give: five checks, or no price.

34
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:21,971
NVDA's multiplier is 1.000775159: already in the price, so Strike never applies it.

35
00:02:21,971 --> 00:02:23,255
The proof page: every claim next to its evidence.

36
00:02:23,255 --> 00:02:26,487
Every deployed contract is verified on Blockscout.

37
00:02:26,487 --> 00:02:29,720
418 Foundry tests, plus Rust, TypeScript, bot and subgraph tests.

38
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:32,936
9 properties proven with Halmos, for every input in range.

39
00:02:32,936 --> 00:02:36,485
An internal review: 11 findings, all fixed, with regression tests.

40
00:02:36,485 --> 00:02:39,849
Strike: options on Robinhood Chain, run by agents that cannot break the rules.

41
00:02:39,849 --> 00:02:43,212
500+ tests, 9 invariants, 9 formal proofs, fork tests on mainnet. github.com/Prashant-thakur77/Strike
